    "proof": {
      "collisionExclusion": "For size m blocks, each signature has N-m+1 ones. Distinct depths therefore cannot collide. Equal-depth disjoint blocks have nonempty zero supports contained in disjoint blocks, so their signatures cannot collide either; the shared bijection preserves these distinctions.",
      "induction": "Current output set is p^{-1}(I). Pulling its query back to original coordinates leaves exactly one marker p[v] inside I, which was registered iff p[v] is in the original left half. Inductively the two child sets are exact, and a leaf writes answer[output]=original=p[output].",
      "fixedCounts": "Each depth has N/2 writes and N reads; no query result is used to change a registration. All registration recursion finishes before one compile, and decoding only starts afterward.",
      "sourceBudgets": {
        "N32": [
          80,
          160
        ],
        "N128": [
          448,
          896
        ],
        "allFiveOriginalBudgetsCovered": true
      },
      "complexity": "Own operations excluding callback bodies O(N^2+NlogN), linear-length callback argument copies O(N^2logN). Parent/sibling candidate-vector lengths on one active branch form a geometric series; buffers are destroyed before descending, so O(N) own space and depth 7 edges/8 frames for N128. All integer counts fit int.",
      "api": "All N/power-of-two and sufficient-method budget checks precede callbacks. N1 still compiles once with no write/read. Function-local lists/buffers and referenced callback objects support independent nested/repeated calls. Concepts require exact void/void/bool return types. Inconsistent side sizes throw; callbacks must still implement the fixed truthful set contract.",
      "adapter": "The by-value adapter string creates its own mutable local before calling the header-declared function, so value/const-reference/mutable-reference library signatures all work without modifying the generic buffer. The actual header is not claimed retrieved; synthetic declarations are only compatibility tests.",
      "exceptions": "Callback and standard allocation exceptions propagate; external side effects are not rolled back. No external session is reused after a failure in the independent recovery checks."
    },
